{"id": "EUVD-2026-81709", "enisaUuid": "0623b601-68a8-37f9-ba94-61de97a74b2c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: mtpav: shut down output timer before card teardown\n\nsnd_mtpav_output_timer() rearms chip->timer while holding\nchip->spinlock and accesses the card-private mtpav state.\n\nsnd_mtpav_free() currently takes the same lock and calls\ntimer_delete() when the timer is active. This only removes a\npending timer; it does not wait for a callback that is already\nrunning and does not prevent the callback from rearming the timer.\n\nA callback running on another CPU can therefore continue after\nsnd_mtpav_free() releases the lock and access the card-private\nstate while the card is being torn down. It can also rearm the\ntimer after timer_delete() has returned.\n\nCall timer_shutdown_sync() without holding chip->spinlock. This\nwaits for any running callback to finish and prevents further\nrearming before the card-private mtpav state is released.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/793163e134028e7136c9dd9e30f7f656de1eabba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/de75857ce374671712e1d9528844e3c0543dcef6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/392c985c6b03dfdf4904c0d464f18735ca3c4df8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e16e82581521a2fe20eda29bdc9e75286f7c950", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c73cb5b7c159246dd572277c668851a56e516019"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f6xw-5hrw-vj32", "CVE-2026-90116"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13ed8292-f297-37a9-b7fa-0f82afa633b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "1b1c3fff-a4b4-32e4-803f-eb33eeb1090b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <793163e134028e7136c9dd9e30f7f656de1eabba"}, {"id": "1f05278d-3f4c-310f-b014-ce5cab423349", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <de75857ce374671712e1d9528844e3c0543dcef6"}, {"id": "35c743b5-03f4-31a3-a806-7b18cea11bc9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "4482462b-1dac-3176-8ead-8c96e33f9454", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <1e16e82581521a2fe20eda29bdc9e75286f7c950"}, {"id": "5b6897ca-ac99-3725-ad36-38fb6934c181", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "5bb6ff14-1d76-343e-bf08-75e86d7dbe37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5c46fe4a-036a-3508-9cd3-e13fe4d5d21d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6a599d71-3c31-3999-9348-863363981a3d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "825cf576-0752-34da-9a85-f344226f9b9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c73cb5b7c159246dd572277c668851a56e516019"}, {"id": "ea2d9227-67a1-3c1a-8ca1-445b3675251a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "f53773ea-f53d-3620-8ae5-2dfee78b2495", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <392c985c6b03dfdf4904c0d464f18735ca3c4df8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7fb3fa01-18c4-31fe-b300-58cac6eb483b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}